constructor appends the required sink column itself, with row \code{x} receiving
sink mass \verb{1 - sum_j matrix[x, j]}, so that the assembled
\verb{n_native x (m + 1)} operator is row-stochastic by construction. A row whose
group mass exceeds one would need negative sink mass and is refused. The
sink column always exists, even when it is identically zero: unmapped
territory has to be a number a reader can see, not an absence.
