\item \code{"density"} divides that by the transported row mass,
\verb{sum_x P[x, j] * row_mass[x]}, giving transported budget per unit
transported territory. A group node reached by no native mass is \code{NA},
never \code{0}. The sink is reported in budget units under either semantics,
because a "density" of unmapped territory has no referent.
